\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Is every group good in the sense of four-dimensional topological surgery? Goodness is the group-theoretic condition that permits the disk-embedding theorem with that fundamental group: algebraically suitable immersed disks in a topological four-manifold can be replaced by embedded disks with the required boundaries and dual spheres. The question quantifies over all groups, rather than only groups of a given growth type.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214441179}{[S2]}.

